      "problem": "Simplify the statement $¬(P∨(Q⇒R)).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that\n\n$$\n¬(P∨(Q⇒R))≡¬(P∨(¬Q∨R)).\n$$\n\nWe can distribute the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(P∨(¬Q∨R)) & ≡¬P∧¬(¬Q∨R) \\\\  & ≡¬P∧(¬(¬Q)∧¬R)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n¬P∧(¬(¬Q)∧¬R)≡¬P∧(Q∧¬R).\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $¬P∧(Q∧¬R)).$",
